From: Paweł Phan <szop.hektar_1w@icloud.com>
Subject: [PATCH] package/libubox, ubus, json-c: build them for the MIPS I variant

SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-only
SPDX-FileCopyrightText: 2026 Paweł Phan <szop.hektar_1w@icloud.com>

The network interface daemon of OpenWrt, netifd, needs libubox, ubus
and json-c. The MIPS I variant of patch 0001 claims no atomic builtins,
so json-c, and ubus with it, are not offered, and libubox builds code
that the core cannot run.

json-c uses one compare-and-swap, to set the seed of its hash tables
once; it uses it only where the compiler defines
__GCC_HAVE_SYNC_COMPARE_AND_SWAP_4, and otherwise stores the value
plainly. Its atomic reference counts are compiled only with
ENABLE_THREADING, which the build system leaves off. The compiler of
the MIPS I variant (gcc configured --without-llsc) defines no such
macro. Offer json-c, and ubus, which depends on the builtins only
because of json-c, to the variant too.

json-c also keeps one value per thread, the format of the numbers it
writes. The variant's toolchain has no threads and emulates
thread-local storage with __emutls_get_address() of libgcc_s, which
json-c would then be the only library to load. Without threads, build
json-c without thread-local storage: the value is the process's.

libubox builds udebug, a ring buffer that processes share and update
with atomic operations; on the variant the compiler turns them into
calls to __atomic_fetch_or_4 and the like, which no library provides.
Add a libubox patch, package/libubox/0001-*.patch, with an option to
leave udebug out, and leave it out on a toolchain without atomics
(BR2_TOOLCHAIN_HAS_ATOMIC unset). ulog() then writes to its other
channels only.

libubox and ubus are taken at OpenWrt's commits of 2026-10-08 and
2026-09-25 (da2d205, 414c60a) instead of those of the release (3868f47
of 2024-12-19, afa57cc of 2025-01-02): procd, which comes next, needs
the newer uloop, and netifd and procd are taken at their current
commits too. ubus's carried patch applies unchanged. The archives'
hashes are computed locally, as the release's were.

Signed-off-by: Paweł Phan <szop.hektar_1w@icloud.com>
---
 package/json-c/Config.in                                                                  |  6 ++++--
 package/json-c/json-c.mk                                                                  |  6 ++++++
 package/libubox/0001-build-make-udebug-optional-for-cores-without-atomic-operations.patch | 70 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 package/libubox/libubox.hash                                                              |  2 +-
 package/libubox/libubox.mk                                                                |  9 ++++++++-
 package/ubus/Config.in                                                                    |  4 ++--
 package/ubus/ubus.hash                                                                    |  2 +-
 package/ubus/ubus.mk                                                                      |  2 +-
 8 files changed, 93 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)

diff --git a/package/json-c/Config.in b/package/json-c/Config.in
index 4df44a9..053a6db 100644
--- a/package/json-c/Config.in
+++ b/package/json-c/Config.in
@@ -1,7 +1,9 @@
 config BR2_PACKAGE_JSON_C
 	bool "json-c"
-	# uses __sync_val_compare_and_swap_4
-	depends on BR2_TOOLCHAIN_HAS_SYNC_4
+	# uses __sync_val_compare_and_swap_4 where the compiler offers
+	# it; the compiler of the MIPS I variant does not, and json-c
+	# then stores the value plainly
+	depends on BR2_TOOLCHAIN_HAS_SYNC_4 || BR2_mips_1
 	help
 	  JSON-C - A JSON implementation in C
 
diff --git a/package/json-c/json-c.mk b/package/json-c/json-c.mk
index 254b6fd..c34a540 100644
--- a/package/json-c/json-c.mk
+++ b/package/json-c/json-c.mk
@@ -12,5 +12,11 @@ JSON_C_LICENSE_FILES = COPYING
 JSON_C_CPE_ID_VENDOR = json-c
 JSON_C_CONF_OPTS = -DBUILD_APPS=OFF -DDISABLE_EXTRA_LIBS=ON
 
+# Without threads a value per thread is a value per process. A toolchain
+# that emulates thread-local storage would take it from libgcc_s.
+ifeq ($(BR2_TOOLCHAIN_HAS_THREADS),)
+JSON_C_CONF_OPTS += -DDISABLE_THREAD_LOCAL_STORAGE=ON
+endif
+
 $(eval $(cmake-package))
 $(eval $(host-cmake-package))
diff --git a/package/libubox/0001-build-make-udebug-optional-for-cores-without-atomic-operations.patch b/package/libubox/0001-build-make-udebug-optional-for-cores-without-atomic-operations.patch
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..9aeb32b
--- /dev/null
+++ b/package/libubox/0001-build-make-udebug-optional-for-cores-without-atomic-operations.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,70 @@
+From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
+From: =?UTF-8?q?Pawe=C5=82=20Phan?= <szop.hektar_1w@icloud.com>
+Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000
+Subject: [PATCH] build: make udebug optional, for cores without atomic
+ operations
+MIME-Version: 1.0
+Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
+Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit
+
+udebug's ring buffer is shared between processes and updated with
+atomic operations (__atomic_fetch_or, __atomic_exchange_n and
+__sync_synchronize). A core that has none, such as a MIPS I core whose
+store-conditional never completes, cannot run that code, and a compiler
+for it makes calls to library functions that no library provides.
+
+Add the option BUILD_UDEBUG, on by default. Off, the library is built
+without udebug.c and udebug-remote.c, and ulog() writes no udebug entry;
+ulog_udebug() still takes a buffer, which is then never written. The
+headers are installed as before.
+
+Upstream: not submitted
+Signed-off-by: Paweł Phan <szop.hektar_1w@icloud.com>
+---
+ CMakeLists.txt | 7 ++++++-
+ ulog.c         | 2 ++
+ 2 files changed, 8 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)
+
+diff --git a/CMakeLists.txt b/CMakeLists.txt
+index bb67fec..f80ecbb 100644
+--- a/CMakeLists.txt
++++ b/CMakeLists.txt
+@@ -13,12 +13,17 @@ ADD_DEFINITIONS(-Os -std=gnu99 -g3 -Wmissing-declarations -Wno-unused-parameter)
+ 
+ OPTION(BUILD_LUA "build Lua plugin" ON)
+ OPTION(BUILD_EXAMPLES "build examples" ON)
++OPTION(BUILD_UDEBUG "build udebug, which needs atomic operations" ON)
+ 
+ INCLUDE(FindPkgConfig)
+ PKG_SEARCH_MODULE(JSONC json-c REQUIRED)
+ INCLUDE_DIRECTORIES(${JSONC_INCLUDE_DIRS})
+ 
+-SET(SOURCES avl.c avl-cmp.c blob.c blobmsg.c uloop.c usock.c ustream.c ustream-fd.c vlist.c utils.c safe_list.c runqueue.c md5.c kvlist.c ulog.c base64.c udebug.c udebug-remote.c)
++SET(SOURCES avl.c avl-cmp.c blob.c blobmsg.c uloop.c usock.c ustream.c ustream-fd.c vlist.c utils.c safe_list.c runqueue.c md5.c kvlist.c ulog.c base64.c)
++IF(BUILD_UDEBUG)
++  LIST(APPEND SOURCES udebug.c udebug-remote.c)
++  ADD_DEFINITIONS(-DUDEBUG)
++ENDIF()
+ 
+ ADD_LIBRARY(ubox SHARED ${SOURCES})
+ ADD_LIBRARY(ubox-static STATIC ${SOURCES})
+diff --git a/ulog.c b/ulog.c
+index 6c2c1f8..3fcef4b 100644
+--- a/ulog.c
++++ b/ulog.c
+@@ -155,6 +155,7 @@ void ulog(int priority, const char *fmt, ...)
+ {
+ 	va_list ap;
+ 
++#ifdef UDEBUG
+ 	if (udb) {
+ 		va_start(ap, fmt);
+ 		udebug_entry_init(udb);
+@@ -162,6 +163,7 @@ void ulog(int priority, const char *fmt, ...)
+ 		udebug_entry_add(udb);
+ 		va_end(ap);
+ 	}
++#endif
+ 
+ 	if (priority > _ulog_threshold)
+ 		return;
diff --git a/package/libubox/libubox.hash b/package/libubox/libubox.hash
index eb37d33..c6fee4f 100644
--- a/package/libubox/libubox.hash
+++ b/package/libubox/libubox.hash
@@ -1,2 +1,2 @@
 # Locally calculated
-sha256  df6e1350fd11016ef30242a279cec195d91e6748c11c40e0991593718c46fa52  libubox-3868f47c8f6c6570e62a3cdf8a7f26ffb1a67e6a-git4.tar.gz
+sha256  402cae56e4dc84cd14f52888f89d565177858d86147f800a16a2d0f15288ea18  libubox-da2d205a5cf3e877c45a2eec488218cbaf452e7d-git4.tar.gz
diff --git a/package/libubox/libubox.mk b/package/libubox/libubox.mk
index 00ae2b0..c0c96e0 100644
--- a/package/libubox/libubox.mk
+++ b/package/libubox/libubox.mk
@@ -4,7 +4,7 @@
 #
 ################################################################################
 
-LIBUBOX_VERSION = 3868f47c8f6c6570e62a3cdf8a7f26ffb1a67e6a
+LIBUBOX_VERSION = da2d205a5cf3e877c45a2eec488218cbaf452e7d
 LIBUBOX_SITE = https://git.openwrt.org/project/libubox.git
 LIBUBOX_SITE_METHOD = git
 LIBUBOX_LICENSE = ISC, BSD-3-Clause
@@ -20,4 +20,11 @@ else
 LIBUBOX_CONF_OPTS += -DBUILD_LUA=OFF
 endif
 
+# udebug updates a buffer shared between processes with atomic operations.
+ifeq ($(BR2_TOOLCHAIN_HAS_ATOMIC),y)
+LIBUBOX_CONF_OPTS += -DBUILD_UDEBUG=ON
+else
+LIBUBOX_CONF_OPTS += -DBUILD_UDEBUG=OFF
+endif
+
 $(eval $(cmake-package))
diff --git a/package/ubus/Config.in b/package/ubus/Config.in
index 391893e..db2164a 100644
--- a/package/ubus/Config.in
+++ b/package/ubus/Config.in
@@ -1,10 +1,10 @@
 comment "ubus needs a toolchain w/ dynamic library"
-	depends on BR2_TOOLCHAIN_HAS_SYNC_4
+	depends on BR2_TOOLCHAIN_HAS_SYNC_4 || BR2_mips_1
 	depends on BR2_STATIC_LIBS
 
 config BR2_PACKAGE_UBUS
 	bool "ubus"
-	depends on BR2_TOOLCHAIN_HAS_SYNC_4 # json-c
+	depends on BR2_TOOLCHAIN_HAS_SYNC_4 || BR2_mips_1 # json-c
 	depends on !BR2_STATIC_LIBS # libubox
 	select BR2_PACKAGE_LIBUBOX
 	select BR2_PACKAGE_JSON_C
diff --git a/package/ubus/ubus.hash b/package/ubus/ubus.hash
index e35f37b..5d0fbec 100644
--- a/package/ubus/ubus.hash
+++ b/package/ubus/ubus.hash
@@ -1,3 +1,3 @@
 # Locally calculated
-sha256  ba7602c660cb2c15c0e04942414e4cf3d96622622406c5fc3b88895694aebb9f  ubus-afa57cce0aff82f4a7a0e509d4387ebc23dd3be7-git4.tar.gz
+sha256  e5409206b54cd44192bd06b386a7d8579ead5001d8b20d7d99c88256c5d7336c  ubus-414c60a2e29e72c2c4f573bc50ad54aef076d169-git4.tar.gz
 sha256  a3caa6c0e90c87b7c97c2ac3d0c0d416082ef777215faec2e9b24ea6e68f6988  ubusd_acl.h
diff --git a/package/ubus/ubus.mk b/package/ubus/ubus.mk
index 913c0e3..68c89b5 100644
--- a/package/ubus/ubus.mk
+++ b/package/ubus/ubus.mk
@@ -4,7 +4,7 @@
 #
 ################################################################################
 
-UBUS_VERSION = afa57cce0aff82f4a7a0e509d4387ebc23dd3be7
+UBUS_VERSION = 414c60a2e29e72c2c4f573bc50ad54aef076d169
 UBUS_SITE = https://git.openwrt.org/project/ubus.git
 UBUS_SITE_METHOD = git
 
